companion.defaultBlipName=Dog
interaction.accompany.promptLabel=Bond
interaction.stay.promptLabel=Stay
interaction.feed.promptLabel=Feed
interaction.praise.promptLabel=Praise
interaction.dismiss.promptLabel=Dismiss
interaction.follow.promptLabel=Follow
interaction.rename.promptLabel=Rename
interaction.attack.promptLabel=Unleash
interaction.retrieve_dog.promptLabel=Retrieve
tutorial.companion_out_of_whistling_range=Your dog is out of your whistling range. Get closer to it and try again, or interact with out primary horse to retrieve it.
tutorial.companion_died=Your dog has died. You cand bond with other dogs and make them your companions.
tutorial.predator_detection=Your dog is getting agitated when there're predators nearby, and it will warn you of them. You can calm it down.
tutorial.fetch=Your dog notices hunted animals and will mark them for you. It won't do that if it's sitting down.
tutorial.companion_low_health=Your dog's health is low. Feed it with hunted prey to heal it.
tutorial.companion_low_health_core=Your dog's health core is low, and it's health will regenerate slower. Feed it with hunted prey to recover it.
tutorial.companion_meal=Feed hunted animals to your dog to refill it's health.
tutorial.companion_wait_outside=Your dog won't follow you inside interiors and won't response to whistles.
tutorial.bond_1=Pat this dog to start bonding with it.
tutorial.bond_2=You can now bond with this dog by pressing ~INPUT_WHISTLE~.
tutorial.bond_3=You now have a dog companion. It will follow you, help you hunt and protect you from threats. Make sure you feed it to maintain its health.
tutorial.tracking=Your dog can track animals quicker than you. Follow it while it's leading you to your tracked animal. To prevent it from doing so, tell it to stay.